# Zig build artifacts. jac/.gitignore covers the in-tree binary build under jac/,
# but `jac run` invoking the native backend emits a .zig-cache/ at the *repo
# root* (its cwd) too -- and a release `git add -A` (release.yml) will
# otherwise sweep in the >100 MB outputs and get rejected by GitHub's file-size
# limit. These patterns are path-anchored to any depth, so they catch both.
.zig-cache/
zig-out/

# c2jac code-reading clones (CPython + pycparser sources, ~194MB) and the P0
# spike -- read-only provenance, never imported by shipping code (pycparser is a
# real jac.toml dependency). Must not land in the repo.
reference/

# Lifted-stub reference corpus: stub modules moved out of the jac-py/jacpython
# import graph (zero callers) but kept verbatim as c2jac reference lifts.
!jac-py/Modules/_lifted/reference/
!jac-py/Modules/_lifted/reference/*.jac

# c2jac sidecar reports are generated next to each input by `jac c2jac` (and by
# running the transpiler over test fixtures) -- generated output, never tracked.
# Baseline sidecar reports are reviewed provenance and stay tracked wherever a
# baseline/ dir or lifted-module dir holds one; everything else is generated
# output next to the transpiler input.
*.c2jac.report.json
!jac-py/tools/**/baseline/project.c2jac.report.json
!jac-py/Modules/_lifted/p1_corpus_slice1b/project.c2jac.report.json
!jac-py/Modules/_lifted/p2_corpus_wave1/project.c2jac.report.json
!jac-py/Modules/_lifted/p2_corpus_wave1/*.jac

# P2 corpus lift staging (ephemeral copies of manifest sources)
jac-py/tools/p2_corpus/_staging/
jac-py/tools/p2_corpus_wave*/_staging/

# Agent / IDE working notes (not repo artifacts)
AGENTS.md
PLAN.md
